<article class="env-lemma" id="087T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/087T">Lemma <span data-tag="087T">30.9.8</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of locally Noetherian schemes. Let $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ X$ be the quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals cutting out $Z$. The functor $i_*$ induces an equivalence between the category of coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules annihilated by $\mathcal{I}$ and the category of coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Z$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The functor is fully faithful by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01QY" data-tag="01QY">29.4.1</a>. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module annihilated by $\mathcal{I}$. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01QY" data-tag="01QY">29.4.1</a> we can write $\mathcal{F} = i_*\mathcal{G}$ for some quasi-coherent sheaf $\mathcal{G}$ on $Z$. By Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01C4" data-tag="01C4">17.13.3</a> we see that $\mathcal{G}$ is of finite type. Hence $\mathcal{G}$ is coherent by Lemma <a href="/tag/01XZ" data-tag="01XZ">30.9.1</a>. Thus the functor is also essentially surjective as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>